# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > b b~ at LO (default coupling orders).
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The only purely strong group in the set. Its flavour union spans both
#     q q~ and g g initial states, so the diagram content reaches colour
#     structures no electroweak-core group does — the s-, t- and u-channel
#     gluon topologies and the triple-gluon vertex feeding a massive quark line
#     — over a proton beam rather than at one fixed flavour assignment.
#   - Massive final-state quarks, so the group also covers the case where the
#     final-state mass, not a cut, is what regulates the phase space.
#
# Not used for amplitudes: no banked b b~ parton row exists. The same colour
# structures are pinned per-diagram and per-flow at other flavours by
# uux_to_uux (q q~ initial state) and gg_to_ttx (g g initial state).
#
# Not used for cross sections or event samples: the run card takes the
# dynamical scale, which the scale layer refuses for want of general kT
# clustering, so both cells are blocked on that feature.
generate p p > b b~
output pp_to_bb -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  done
